{
 "_doc": {
  "zh": "第二层（负荷估计）在有已知答案的姿势上的结果，由 tools/activity/validate.ts 生成。判定只看名次和符号：应当用力的肌肉激活度 > 0.5% 且高于应当安静的肌肉，要求力矩的符号正确。激活度的数值本身不可信（见 params.json 里的假设）。",
  "en": "Results of layer 2 (the load estimate) on the poses with known answers, written by tools/activity/validate.ts. Only ranks and signs are judged: muscles expected to work are above 0.5 % and above those expected to stay silent, and the required torque has the right sign. The activation numbers themselves are not to be trusted (see the assumptions in params.json)."
 },
 "cases": [
  {
   "id": "elbow90",
   "name": {
    "zh": "屈肘 90°，前臂水平",
    "en": "elbow flexed 90°, forearm horizontal"
   },
   "gravity": "stand",
   "load": null,
   "basis": {
    "zh": "重力使前臂下落（伸肘），由屈肘肌对抗",
    "en": "gravity drops the forearm (extends the elbow); the elbow flexors oppose it"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "elbow90load",
   "name": {
    "zh": "屈肘 90°，手持 2 kg",
    "en": "elbow flexed 90° holding 2 kg"
   },
   "gravity": "stand",
   "load": {
    "kg": 2,
    "side": "B"
   },
   "basis": {
    "zh": "同上，负荷更大，激活度应更高",
    "en": "as above with more load: activations must be higher"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "overhead",
   "name": {
    "zh": "上臂举过头、屈肘 70°",
    "en": "arm overhead, elbow flexed 70°"
   },
   "gravity": "stand",
   "load": null,
   "basis": {
    "zh": "前臂在肘的上方，重力使肘屈曲，由伸肘肌对抗",
    "en": "the forearm is above the elbow, gravity flexes it and the elbow extensors oppose it"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "abduction90",
   "name": {
    "zh": "肩外展 90°",
    "en": "arm abducted 90°"
   },
   "gravity": "stand",
   "load": null,
   "basis": {
    "zh": "重力使上臂内收，由三角肌中束和冈上肌对抗",
    "en": "gravity adducts the arm; the middle deltoid and supraspinatus oppose it"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "squat",
   "name": {
    "zh": "浅蹲（屈膝 60°）",
    "en": "shallow squat (knees 60°)"
   },
   "gravity": "stand",
   "load": null,
   "basis": {
    "zh": "体重使膝屈曲，由股四头肌对抗；只跨膝关节的屈膝肌（股二头肌短头、腘肌）应当安静。躯干前倾时跨髋和膝的腘绳肌会作为伸髋肌一起用力，所以不把它们列为\"应当安静\"",
    "en": "body weight flexes the knees and the quadriceps oppose it; the knee flexors that span the knee alone (short head of biceps femoris, popliteus) must stay silent. With the trunk leaning forward the two-joint hamstrings work as hip extensors, so they are not listed as silent"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "tiptoe",
   "name": {
    "zh": "踮脚站立",
    "en": "standing on tiptoe"
   },
   "gravity": "stand",
   "load": null,
   "basis": {
    "zh": "地面反力在前足，使踝背屈，由小腿三头肌对抗",
    "en": "the ground reaction under the forefoot dorsiflexes the ankle; the triceps surae opposes it"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "lean",
   "name": {
    "zh": "以踝为轴前倾 6°",
    "en": "leaning forward 6° at the ankles"
   },
   "gravity": "stand",
   "load": null,
   "basis": {
    "zh": "重心移到踝的前方，由跖屈肌拉住",
    "en": "the centre of mass moves in front of the ankles and the plantar flexors hold it"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "trunk30",
   "name": {
    "zh": "躯干前屈 30°",
    "en": "trunk flexed forward 30°"
   },
   "gravity": "stand",
   "load": null,
   "basis": {
    "zh": "上身重量使脊柱前屈，由竖脊肌对抗",
    "en": "the weight of the upper body flexes the spine; the erector spinae opposes it"
   }
  },
  {
